    "explanation": "To both parties: the record supports this no-show charge, the rider's SGD 4.50 fee stands and is not refunded, and the platform pays the driver SGD 3.60.\n\nArrival and dwell (POL-NS-01). The trip record shows driver DRV-09728 tapping 'I'm Here' at 21:26:22 and the 180-second wait timer starting at 21:26:24. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02728) places him inside the STANDARD-zone arrival radius of 50 m of the pin on a single continuous qualifying run of 436 seconds, from 21:26:22 to 21:33:38, across 45 qualifying fixes, with a closest approach of 0.11 m. That is 256 seconds more than the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec). Limbs (a), (b) and (c) are therefore met, and no_show_threshold_sec is null so no longer threshold applies. The arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05: at the marker the driver was stationary at the pin, neither more than 300 m away nor travelling at 15 km/h or above; the recomputed clock therefore starts where the record says it does. The driver cancelled at 21:33:39 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the dwell had elapsed and with no boarding event anywhere in the record, so limb (d) is met.\n\nNo displacing clause. POL-NS-02 is satisfied, since qualifying in-radius fixes exist, so it does not refund the fee. POL-NS-03 does not apply: the driver's stationary fixes were inside the 50 m radius, not outside it, so this is not a wrong-entrance case and no pin-ambiguity goodwill arises. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: the chat log (EV-CHAT-02728) holds one message and it is the driver's ('im at the pickup point', sent 21:26:42, read 21:27:12); the rider sent nothing in the waiting window, so limb (a) fails, and the rider's device track shows zero qualifying fixes inside the 100 m rider-presence radius with a closest fix 797.9 m from the pin, so limb (c) fails too. POL-NS-06 does not apply: the 436-second dwell exceeds the 180-second minimum, so there is no shortfall and nothing to refund; the missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02728-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) is irrelevant for that reason, and neither side may use it, so the two claims that cited it without naming its issue code were discarded by the referee. POL-NS-10 does not apply: the driver, not the rider, terminated the trip.\n\nThe fee and the payout. The fare ledger (EV-FARE-02728) charges a single cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.50 and no waiting-time line, reconciling with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of SGD 4.50, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare-integrity defect and the amount charged is the correct net figure. Under POL-NS-07 the driver is compensated at 80% of that net fee: SGD 3.60. The anti-farming check does not trip, because both limbs must hold and the first does not: no_show_terminations_30d is 3 (below 4) and 3 divided by 40 completed trips is 0.075 (below 0.08). No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger fires: the deciding facts rest on artifacts at full weight 1.0 (trip record, GPS trace), so confidence is above the 0.70 floor; no admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival or dwell; no counterparty disputes appear in the trailing 90 days; and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0. Nothing in the driver or rider profile is used as a ground of decision.\n\nBoth advocates' surviving claims on the four limbs, the fare integrity, the false-arrival test and the anti-farming check are accepted and lead to this outcome. The rider's claim that the driver 'cancelled on me again' is not supported on this record. The monetary effect (SGD 3.60) is below the execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so it executes automatically on issue; the disputed SGD 4.50 charge is left as it is, and SGD 3.60 is paid to the driver."
