    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02728 stands unchanged, and the driver is paid SGD 3.60 of it.\n\nWHY THE FEE STANDS. Under POL-NS-01 a no-show fee is chargeable only where all four conditions hold, and on this record they do. (a) The trip record (EV-TRIP-02728) carries the driver's 'I'm Here' arrival event at 21:26:22. (b) The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02728) puts him at the pickup pin - minimum distance 0.11 m - with 45 qualifying fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius required by POL-NS-02, the first of them at 21:26:22, the same moment as the tap. That also disposes of POL-NS-05: the arrival marker was not false (he was at the pin, stationary, at the marker's timestamp), so the waiting clock runs from 21:26:22 exactly as the record states. (c) He then held position continuously from 21:26:22 to 21:33:38 - 436 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period in this trip's own platform_policy - which is 256 seconds more than the minimum, so POL-NS-06's shortfall clause has nothing to bite on. (d) No boarding event is recorded and the driver terminated the trip at 21:33:39 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the dwell had elapsed.\n\nWHAT DOES NOT DISPLACE THE FEE. POL-NS-03 is the wrong-entrance clause and does not apply: the driver's stationary fixes were inside the arrival radius, not outside it, so there is no wrong-face-of-the-building case and no pin-ambiguity goodwill. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider: limb (a) requires a locating or coordinating message from the rider, and the chat log (EV-CHAT-02728) holds only the driver's message at 21:26:42, 'im at the pickup point', read at 21:27:12 - the rider sent nothing during the waiting window. Independently, the rider's own 76-fix device track never comes closer than 797.9 m to the pin (mean 802.0 m), so limb (c) fails on its merits as well; and POL-NS-11 would not change the result even if that limb were treated as unrunnable, because the fee would then be decided on the driver's evidence, which is complete. POL-NS-10 concerns cancellations the rider makes; this trip was terminated by the driver, so its grace and waiting-time limbs do not bear on this fee. On integrity (POL-NS-08): the fare line of SGD 4.50 equals the platform_policy cancellation fee in force, so limb (d) finds no fare defect; the arrival timestamp matches a GPS fix at zero offset, there are no sampling gaps (0.0 s maximum gap, 100 per cent coverage, 87 driver fixes), and the chat log is complete against the record's own message count, so nothing is impaired.\n\nTHE MONEY. Because POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 per cent of the SGD 4.50 fee in force - SGD 3.60 - the residual SGD 0.90 being retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is 3, below the threshold of 4, and 3 divided by 40 completed trips is 0.075, below the 0.08 rate; both limbs must be met before compensation is withheld, and neither is. The ruling is therefore DRIVER_COMPENSATION, and per POL-GEN-03 amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.60 - that is the amount the ruling moves, not a second payment, and no refund goes to the rider. The monetary effect, SGD 3.60, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so under POL-GEN-05 it executes automatically on issue.\n\nESCALATION AND REFERRALS. No POL-NS-09 trigger is engaged: confidence is above the 0.70 floor; the trip record and the GPS trace agree on arrival and dwell rather than contradicting each other; neither party shows disputes with the other counterparty in the trailing 90 days; the anti-farming check does not trip and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0; and no deciding fact rests on an artifact impaired under POL-NS-08. No clause produces a referral here: POL-NS-05(ii) does not fire because the arrival marker was true, and POL-NS-07's escalation packet